      },
      "description": "Average correlation of every in-brain voxel with the global mean timeseries, matching AFNI's @compute_gcor. Elevated GCOR means a signal common to the whole brain is dominating — typically motion or respiration rather than neural activity. Descriptive: compare across the cohort, no fixed cutoff. Note the emitter records 0.0 when the IQM computation fails, so an exact 0.000 means 'not measured', not 'no global signal'.",
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center",
