      },
      "description": "Median temporal SNR per run. Unlike motion, this is driven mostly by the acquisition itself — sequence, coil, and run length — so a batch from one site tends to form a tight cluster. A low-tSNR tail that does NOT coincide with the high-motion tail usually indicates an acquisition problem, not a restless participant.",
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "filterFieldsByName",
          "options": {
